# About ↔ README sync

The in-game **About** screen (`src/ui/licenses_panel.gd`, `_text_ko()` / `_text_en()`) and the **About** section of `README.md` must stay aligned.

## When to update both

Any change to credits, disclaimers, third-party licenses, URLs, or AI-usage wording in either file requires the same change in the other in the **same edit**.

## How to mirror content

| In-game About | README.md |
|---------------|-----------|
| `_text_ko()` | Korean blocks under `## About` (before the English `### Ultima IV (DOS) game data` section) |
| `_text_en()` | English blocks under `## About` (from `### Ultima IV (DOS) game data` through `### AI usage`) |

Keep section order and meaning the same. README may use `###` headings and markdown links; About uses plain text with URLs on their own lines — wording should match.

## Checklist before finishing

1. Every section in `_text_ko()` / `_text_en()` has a README counterpart (e.g. xu4, libhangul, Godot, u4graphics, **Apple II**, Raven, Freesound, music, D2Coding, disclaimer, AI).
2. No About-only or README-only attribution left behind.
3. If GOG / game-data requirements change in About, also update `## 플레이하려면` / `## To play` in README when relevant.

## Source of truth

Prefer editing `licenses_panel.gd` first (player-facing), then copy the substance into `README.md`.
